    {
      "beat_id": "B02B",
      "act": "The objective",
      "narration_text": "The tool checks itself here, too. Chapter fifteen sets a skip rate target of at least fifty percent — how many companies should get filtered out before they are even scored. This run skips only thirty-one point five percent. That is reported as a dial, not enforced as a rule, because tightening it until the number looks right would just be optimizing the dial instead of the decision.",
